Step 1 — Install Tomcat
cd /opt
wget https://dlcdn.apache.org/tomcat/tomcat-9/v9.0.98/bin/apache-tomcat-9.0.98.tar.gz
tar -xvzf apache-tomcat-9.0.98.tar.gz
mv apache-tomcat-9.0.98 tomcat

Check tomcat.apache.org/download-90.cgi for the current version number and swap it in if different.

Step 2 — Start Tomcat (default port 8080) and verify
/opt/tomcat/bin/startup.sh

Give it a few seconds, then confirm it's actually listening:
netstat -tulnp | grep 8080

(if netstat isn't found: yum install net-tools -y first)

Step 3 — Deploy WAR from Question 4
cp ~/2026b-cosc2767-a1-<repo-name>/question-4/my_project/target/mywebsite-s123456.war /opt/tomcat/webapps/
Tomcat auto-unpacks it within a few seconds — confirm:
ls /opt/tomcat/webapps/
both mywebsite-s123456.war and a matching unpacked folder mywebsite-s123456/.

Step 4 — Open port 8080 in the Security Group

In AWS Console: EC2 → Security Groups → instance's SG → Inbound rules → Edit inbound rules → Add rule
Type: Custom TCP, Port: 8080, Source: Anywhere (0.0.0.0/0)
Save rules

Step 5 — Access on 8080
In browser:
http://<EC2-Public-IP>:8080/mywebsite-s123456/

Step 6 — Reconfigure Tomcat to 9xxx port
Figure out port first: last 3 digits of student ID, prefixed with 9.

/opt/tomcat/bin/shutdown.sh
nano /opt/tomcat/conf/server.xml
Find this line (search with Ctrl+W in nano):
<Connector port="8080" protocol="HTTP/1.1"

Change 8080 to assigned port, e.g.:
<Connector port="9456" protocol="HTTP/1.1"

Save (Ctrl+X, Y, Enter), then restart:
/opt/tomcat/bin/startup.sh

Step 7 — Open 9xxx port in the Security Group
Same as Step 4, but this time: Type Custom TCP, Port 9456 (actual port), Source Anywhere.

Step 8 — Access on the new port
http://<EC2-Public-IP>:9456/mywebsite-s123456/

Step 9 — ecurity Group inbound rules → 5c.png
AWS Console → EC2 → Security Groups → SG → Inbound rules tab. This should now show both 8080 and 9xxx port (plus 22 for SSH, and anything from earlier questions).

Step 10 — Copy server.xml into repo and commit
mkdir -p ~/2026b-cosc2767-a1-<repo-name>/question-5
cp /opt/tomcat/conf/server.xml ~/2026b-cosc2767-a1-<repo-name>/question-5/
cd ~/2026b-cosc2767-a1-<repo-name>
git checkout develop
git add question-5/server.xml
git status
git commit -m "Configure Tomcat to run on the port 9xxx"
git push
